Process Worker back-pressure fix: local before/after (post-freeze, 6 November 2026).

Setup (bp.ps1 in this folder)
  Scratch Compose project flashsale-bp, new volumes, removed after each run.
  - Env: the EC2 values (Worker concurrency 20, prefetch 20, Order consumers 4,
    reconciliation 120 s for PendingStock and 300 s for Confirmed/Processing).
  - Version frozen: a clone at 9d00bea (tag w14-official).
  - Version fix: a clone of dfb0cd5 with the working tree's Process Worker
    (PublishBackPressure).
  - To make the Order Service queues fill on this PC, as they do on the 2-vCPU EC2 host:
    queue bound 20 (-QueueMaxLength 20), Order Service limited to 0.5 CPU, C3 at 200/s
    for 60 s.
  This is a deliberately starved setup, far harsher than EC2 (bound 1000), so its absolute
  times are not EC2 numbers.
  Worker dead letters are the peak depth of ProcessWorker.StockReserved.dlq (local runs
  export no service metrics to the collector). Back-pressure waits are read from the
  Worker's /metrics; re-triggers from the OrderPlaced Outbox rows; stuck states from
  Order Service's log.

Results (frozen-1.log, frozen-2.log, fix-1.log, fix-2.log)
  run        accepted  worker dead letters  back-pressure waits  re-triggers (state)                     drain   validator
  frozen 1   608       1                    (not exported)       (not measured; harness not yet updated)  304 s   PASS
  frozen 2   645       3                    (not exported)       7 (Processing 6, Confirmed 1)            333 s   PASS
  fix 1      829       0                    245                  3 (state not recorded)                   314 s   PASS
  fix 2      641       0                    236                  3 (Processing 2, Confirmed 1)            306 s   PASS

Reading
  The defect reproduces on the frozen code: the Worker dead-letters StockReserved when an
  Order Service queue is full, and those orders complete only through reconciliation.
  The fix removes the dead letters in both runs, and the Worker waits instead (236-245
  waits), with every validator check holding.
  On this starved stack a few held orders still wait longer than the 300 s
  Confirmed/Processing timeout, so reconciliation still re-triggers them (3 against 7)
  and the drain stays near 300 s. The fix removes the defect but not, here, the tail; the
  reconciliation timeout was not changed. Whether the tail goes on EC2 (bound 1000, no
  CPU limit) is what docs/week14-backpressure-fix.md measures.
Exit code: 0

Regression checks on the fix (a clone of dfb0cd5 with the fixed Process Worker, built on E:)
  unit-tests.log        7 of 7: nack -> back-pressure; return or any other error -> ladder;
                        waits do not use attempts; the wait cap rethrows; cancellation stops waiting
  verify-worker.log     TP-P01, 56 of 56 PASS (deterministic work, one completion per order under
                        replay, restart and reordering, no DLQ)
  verify-failures.log   TP-F01, 74 of 74 PASS (bounded retries; poison and exhausted messages,
                        Worker included, still reach the right DLQ)
